An analysis of the build failure indicates that the test `tests/subsys/dfu/img_util` is being built with a sysbuild configuration that makes it a child image of MCUboot. In this scenario, `CONFIG_IMG_MANAGER` is disabled for the application, which in turn disables `CONFIG_MCUBOOT_IMG_MANAGER`.

The compilation fails because the public header `include/zephyr/dfu/flash_img.h` uses `CONFIG_IMG_BLOCK_BUF_SIZE`, which is only defined when `CONFIG_MCUBOOT_IMG_MANAGER` is enabled. This makes the header unsafe to include when the feature is disabled.

The fix involves two parts:
1.  Make the `flash_img.h` header safe by wrapping the API declarations (structs and function prototypes) in a `#if defined(CONFIG_MCUBOOT_IMG_MANAGER) || defined(__DOXYGEN__)` block. This ensures that including the header does not cause a build failure when the underlying feature is disabled.
2.  Modify the test source file `tests/subsys/dfu/img_util/src/main.c` to handle the case where `CONFIG_MCUBOOT_IMG_MANAGER` is not defined. The test code, which relies on the `flash_img` API, is wrapped in a similar conditional compilation block. An `#else` branch is added to provide a stub test that skips execution, ensuring the test suite can still be built and report a skip for the invalid configuration.

These changes resolve the build error and make the test case robust to different build configurations.

